A||||1||Homicidal||OMG!  I actually FIXED something on MY Fiero!!!!!!!||||10||
Z||000000||Homicidal||05-08-2000||10:58 PM||||That weird "bucking" and starting problem is now gone!  I thought it was the battery so I bought a new one, something I was planning to do anyways.  But it still didn't work.  I decided to get dirty and climb under the car and have a looksy.  I found out a starter cable was extremely loose than what it should have been.<P>I jacked my baby up, tighented it and viola, no more troubles!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||Coconut||05-08-2000||11:27 PM||||Yeah, That's the real beauty of being the Do-it-yourselfer! When you finally decide that there's no other way than to "get under the darn thing" and try to figure out what the heck is going on!  Like I said in my other post I'm a terrible trouble shooter, but it feels pretty good to know you're able to fix it yourself(with the advice of those who have "been there,done that") and not have to fork over your hard earned dough to somebody. There is an abundance of knowledge and experience on this site and I plan to utilize it to it's full capacity. Congratulations on one of your victories  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    Keep Cruising, Coconut <p>[This message has been edited by Coconut (edited 05-08-2000).]||||reg||14
